<addAttributes>
    <att name='institution'>McGill University</att>
    <att name='title'>Pacific eDNA Coastal Observatory (PECO)</att>
    <att name='summary'>The Pacific eDNA Coastal Observatory (PECO) is a coordinated network of partners using environmental DNA to track changes in marine biodiversity through time. Our network spans 26 degrees latitude (Alaska to Southern California), in a cross-national region of high economic and social interest in marine resource management. The goals of this project are to develop tools, platforms and networks to enable the use of environmental DNA for broad-scale biogeographic assessment, build capacity to track biodiversity changes through time, and connect users with updatable predictive tools on biodiversity changes. This package describes the data collected between 2021-2024. NOTE: some of the raw DNA sequences are derived from samples collected on Haida territory by the Council of the Haida Nation (CHN). These samples were provided for the sole purpose of this research, and require permission before further use. All research conducted on, or in relation to, Haida territory is subject to a Council of the Haida Nation Research Permit, with the exception of research carried out in partnership with the CHN or Gwaii Haanas</att>
    <att name='project'>Nearshore,Genomics</att>
